---
// The cutting desk: the double-wonks, each with its plate and a door to its cusps.
//
// The operator, 2026-11-23: "i dont really like many of the double-wonkies because they are too
// anthropomorphic or zoomorphic. many of them i want to cut at the big blue dot."
//
// This page lists only the records that can be cut: a name beginning "double-" with stored
// points. The list comes from the registry, never from a typed set of uids. The rule and the
// cut itself are app/src/lib/cut-doubles.js; the save is /api/cut-double.
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { loadRegistry } from "../../lib/registry.ts";
import { cuspsOf, doublesOf } from "../../lib/cut-doubles.js";

const registry = await loadRegistry();
const doubles = doublesOf(registry.curves).map((curve) => ({
  uid: curve.uid,
  name: curve.name,
  cusps: cuspsOf(curve.path).length,
}));
const ready = doubles.filter((curve) => curve.cusps > 0);
---

<BaseLayout title="the cut desk" pageTitle="The cut desk">
  <p class="lead">The double-wonkies, {doubles.length} of them, and the dot to cut at. A double
    is cut where it crosses <code>y = x</code> and mirrored back, so each carries a seam of
    cusps; the plate marks each one with a bigger blue dot. Open one and choose the dot: the
    long arc is kept, the lobe the dot closes is dropped, and the cut is saved as a new curve
    beside its parent — the parent is never changed.</p>
  <p class="lead">{ready.length} have a cusp to cut at; the others are listed but say so.
    To cut a curve's legs off at a rational fraction of t instead, use
    <a href="/trim/">the trim desk</a>.</p>

  <div class="cut-grid">
    {doubles.map((curve) => (
      <figure class="cut-card">
        <a href={`/cut/${curve.uid}`}>
          <img src={`/plates-web/${curve.uid}-1600-grey.png`} alt={`the plate of ${curve.uid} ${curve.name}`}
            width="1600" height="800" loading="lazy" />
        </a>
        <figcaption>
          <a href={`/cut/${curve.uid}`}><code>{curve.uid}</code> {curve.name}</a>
          <span class="cut-note">{curve.cusps > 0
            ? `${curve.cusps} cusp${curve.cusps === 1 ? "" : "s"}`
            : "no cusp"} · <a href={`/trim/${curve.uid}`}>trim the legs</a></span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    ))}
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style is:global>
  .cut-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(20rem, 1fr)); gap: 14px; }
  .cut-card { margin: 0; border: 1px solid #e6dccb; background: #fff; padding: 6px; }
  .cut-card img { display: block; width: 100%; height: 150px; object-fit: contain; background: #fff; }
  .cut-card figcaption { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 8px; align-items: baseline;
    margin-top: 6px; font: 12px/1.4 ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; }
  .cut-note { color: #7a6a55; }
</style>
